{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b341c4557dcf8470","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Llama Stack GA-Readiness Assessment\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: the full inventory of gaps\n30\tbetween current Llama Stack Tech Preview quality and the GA bar. It produces\n31\tthe definitive GA scope that all Llama Stack stability, hardening, and support\n32\tposture work is sized against. Until this assessment lands, the size of the\n33\tstability and hardening work remains an estimate (strategy Open Question 1).\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Systematically inventory gaps between current TP quality and the GA bar\n38\t  across the four assessment dimensions named in the strategy:\n39\t  - API stability (which parts of the published OpenAI-compatible API surface\n40\t    and LlamaStackDistribution CRD behavior are unstable or undocumented)\n41\t  - Upgrade paths (what breaks when moving between recent TP releases)\n42\t  - Scale limits (documented and observed limits of supported distributions)\n43\t  - Error handling (failure modes, error surfacing, recovery behavior)\n44\t- Consolidate scattered TP feedback from support tickets into the gap\n45\t  inventory.\n46\t- Produce the definitive GA scope document: each gap classified\n47\t  (must-fix-for-GA vs. acceptable-with-follow-up), with the remediation work\n48\t  itemized so downstream implementation epics can be sized and scoped.\n49\t- Identify which gaps fall into API stabilization work, which into general\n50\t  hardening, and which constrain the supported configuration matrix and SLO\n51\t  targets.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A gap inventory exists covering all four assessment dimensions (API\n56\t  stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with each gap\n57\t  traceable to evidence (source inspection, upgrade testing, or support\n58\t  ticket).\n59\t- TP feedback from support tickets is consolidated and reflected in the\n60\t  inventory.\n61\t- A definitive GA scope document is produced that downstream stability,\n62\t  hardening, and support-posture work can be scoped from, with each GA-blocking\n63\t  gap assigned to a remediation area.\n64\t- Gaps that inform the supported configuration matrix and SLO targets are\n65\t  explicitly called out.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0): GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current TP\n70\t  quality and GA bar, producing the definitive GA scope. This epic is the\n71\t  assessment itself.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf6e1d0d1832fc50","agent_id":"a69dc72ccb749c3c1","session_id":"24dada96-80a8-453c-92a4-331603e90011","uuid":"5e37441d-cd05-4418-89b3-112afcf7191a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:02:27.230Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b341c4557dcf8470","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
