{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9e742f1d8aa573e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack API stability guarantee and tested upgrade path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the GA-readiness assessment finds the API surface already\n15\t    largely stable, scope narrows to versioning, the deprecation policy, and upgrade-path\n16\t    testing; if it finds deeper instability, the stabilization scope expands and the\n17\t    GA timeline must be re-planned.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Llama Stack API Stability Guarantee and Tested Upgrade Path\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic delivers the API stability guarantee that GA requires for the\n40\tLlama Stack published API surface: versioned APIs, a deprecation policy, and\n41\ta tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Version the published API surface (the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the\n46\t  LlamaStackDistribution CRD behavior exposed to users) so GA customers can\n47\t  build against a stable contract.\n48\t- Author and publish a deprecation policy defining how API changes are\n49\t  signaled, how long deprecated surfaces remain supported, and what customers\n50\t  must do when upgrading.\n51\t- Implement and test an upgrade path from the last two TP releases to the GA\n52\t  release, including migration of existing LlamaStackDistribution resources.\n53\t- Stabilize the specific API behaviors flagged as GA-blocking by the\n54\t  GA-readiness assessment.\n55\t- Keep the existing Konflux build pipeline green for all changes in the\n56\t  Llama Stack midstream repo.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Published APIs are versioned, and the versioning scheme is documented.\n61\t- A deprecation policy is published and covers signaling, support windows for\n62\t  deprecated surfaces, and upgrade obligations.\n63\t- An upgrade from each of the last two TP releases to the GA release is\n64\t  exercised by automated tests, with documented migration steps for any\n65\t  breaking change.\n66\t- API behaviors identified as GA-blocking by the GA-readiness assessment are\n67\t  stabilized or explicitly covered by the deprecation policy.\n68\t- The Konflux build pipeline for the Llama Stack midstream repo is green with\n69\t  these changes.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-2 (P0): Published API surface carries a stability guarantee — versioned\n74\t  APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP\n75\t  releases.\n76\t- HLR-1 (P0, partial): stabilization targets are the API-stability gaps\n77\t  inventoried by the GA-readiness assessment.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf6e1d0d1832fc50","agent_id":"a69dc72ccb749c3c1","session_id":"24dada96-80a8-453c-92a4-331603e90011","uuid":"5d3fe2c1-9e99-41c2-8153-c6dbbd2b1dac","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:02:27.936Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9e742f1d8aa573e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
