 Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- On an entitled cluster with default configuration, Llama Stack management\n55\t  is available in the Dashboard with no opt-in action required.\n56\t- On clusters without entitlement, the capability remains hidden.\n57\t- The capability can be explicitly disabled via configuration by an\n58\t  administrator (rollback for the default change).\n59\t- The Konflux build pipeline for the Dashboard repo is green with these\n60\t  changes.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-5 (P1): The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n65\t  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate).\n66\t\n67\t## Notes\n68\t\n69\tRelease coordination: this change exposes Llama Stack management to all\n70\tentitled clusters, so it should ship in step with the Llama Stack GA\n71\tgraduation rather than ahead of it. This is a release-train coordination\n72\tpoint, not a code dependency — the Dashboard change builds against the\n73\talready-existing LlamaStackDistribution CR surface and is otherwise\n74\tindependent.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf6e1d0d1832fc50","agent_id":"a69dc72ccb749c3c1","session_id":"24dada96-80a8-453c-92a4-331603e90011","uuid":"c172ce35-b2e9-48ee-8ee1-036fdbd35fe0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:02:34.344Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-85cbb6d953182486","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
