\n170\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n171\t\n172\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from HLR text. Rule-mandated ACs are all\n173\tpresent where applicable:\n174\t\n175\t- Rollback/feature-flag (E007, the default-flip change): \"The capability can\n176\t  be explicitly disabled via configuration by an administrator (rollback for\n177\t  the default change).\"\n178\t- Technical review (E008, docs-authoring): \"All GA documentation is\n179\t  technically reviewed against the implemented behavior by the owning\n180\t  engineering teams before publication.\"\n181\t- Build pipeline green: E002, E003, E005, and E007 all carry \"the Konflux\n182\t  build pipeline ... is green with these changes\" ACs (no konflux-onboarding\n183\t  epic exists in any dependency chain, so the AC is not strictly mandated,\n184\t  but its presence is correct and conservative). E004 and E006 have no repo\n185\t  code changes, so its absence there is fine.\n186\t\n187\tNo epic body references sibling epics by draft ID — cross-epic references use\n188\twork names (\"the GA-readiness assessment\", \"the GA documentation uplift\"),\n189\twhich survive Jira translation.\n190\t\n191\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n192\t\n193\tAll strategy scope is covered: every HLR sub-deliverable checks out against\n194\tthe combined epic set (HLR-2's versioned APIs / deprecation policy / upgrade\n195\tpath from last two TP releases → E002 + E008 migration notes; HLR-3's SLOs /\n196\tbackport policy / config matrix → E004 + E008 customer-facing content; HLR-4\n197\t→ E005 + E006 + E008; HLR-5 → E007; HLR-6 → E008). E001's four assessment\n198\tdimensions are each consumed downstream (API stability → E002; upgrade paths\n199\t→ E002; scale limits/error handling → E003 + E004). Out-of-scope constraints\n200\tare respected (E003 is GA-bar remediation, not new feature work). Strategy\n201\tOpen Question 1 is modeled as E001 and carried into downstream gates rather\n202\tthan dropped; the missing strategy sections (Impacted Teams, Dependencies,\n203\tNFRs, Staff Engineer Input) are flagged in Health Warnings with the inferred\n204\tteam assignments called out for human confirmation, not silently dropped.\n205\tThe strategy has no Prerequisites & Process Gates section declaring\n206\t`Documentation Support`, but HLR-6 explicitly requires documentation uplift,\n207\tand E008 (docs-authoring) covers it. Conditional branches are correctly\n208\tomitted: E001's outcome (an unbounded gap inventory) cannot be enumerated as\n209\t≤3 bounded outcomes, and the decomposition correctly uses phased\n210\tdecomposition with `gated_by` on E002/E003/E004 per Rule 3.\n211\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89922ab9343ab5e2","agent_id":"aa34066a390b7dfa5","session_id":"24dada96-80a8-453c-92a4-331603e90011","uuid":"b214e111-dbd6-4585-a599-81491db0b83f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:08:43.129Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5b8e0b48f1ad936","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
