ent, matching the convention. No cycles, no\nedges referencing nonexistent epics, no branch files (and none required — see\nCriterion 7). No `konflux-onboarding` epics exist (all three components are\nalready onboarded midstream per architecture context), so the rule 7/8/10\nparallelism constraints are vacuously satisfied; the \"pipeline green\" ACs in\nE002/E003/E005/E007 are AC gates, not DAG edges — correct.\n\nEdge justification review: E001 → E002/E003/E004 are Rule 3 investigation\ngates backed by strategy Open Question 1. E005 → E006 is a producer→consumer\nedge across teams. E004 → E006 is a content dependency (E006 validates against\nthe supported-configuration matrix and support posture E004 publishes) —\njustified. E002 → E004 is a genuine content dependency (the backport policy\ndocuments commitments against the versioned API surface and deprecation\npolicy); noted as a minor below because it also blocks the SLO/config-matrix\nhalf of E004 which only needs E001. Deliberately absent edges (no edges into\nE007; no E005 ↔ E002/E003/E004 chain) are each argued from the rules and are\ncorrect — HLR-4 and HLR-5 are independent of the assessment outcome and live\nin distinct work areas/repos. Critical path (E001→E002→E004→E006→E008, length\n5) is within the L-strategy heuristic (5-7) for a 3-component, 6-HLR strategy.\nNo data/artifact dependency discoverable from epic content is missing from the\nDAG: E006's hand-off to the docs uplift is captured as E006 → E008, and E008's\nmigration-notes alignment on the upgrade path is captured as E002 → E008.\n\nMinor (does not reduce score): the E002 → E004 edge serializes all of E004 on\nE002, but only the backport policy consumes E002's output; SLO targets and the\nsupported configuration matrix depend only on E001's findings. The edge is\naccepted as a justified Rule 13 content dependency and does not materially\nchange execution order (E004 already waits on E001).\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n\nEach epic is a cle